<title>USA: American Coin closes cheaper credit line.</title>
<headline>American Coin closes cheaper credit line.</headline>
<dateline>BOULDER, Colo. 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Coin Merchandising Inc said on Tuesday it had closed a $6 million multiyear revolving credit facility priced at the prime rate, to finance its working capital requirements and spending.</p>
<p>American Coin said it had previously borrowed at the prime rate plus 0.5 percent.</p>
<p>The coin-operated skill-crane machine operator said in a statement it closed the line with Wells Fargo Bank.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
